## 1. Capacity handling — the current mechanism

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureCityCapacity.java`** — the only place the `50` limit and city-based counting live. Full body:

```java
public class EnsureCityCapacity {

    private static final int CAPACITY = 50;

    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws CityAtCapacityException {
        String city = owner.getCity();
        int count = 0;
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (city != null && city.equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getCity())) {
                count++;
            }
        }
        if (count >= CAPACITY) {
            throw new CityAtCapacityException(city, count);
        }
    }
}
```

This is where **owner-counting-by-city currently happens**: it iterates `OwnerRepository.findAll()` in-memory and compares `city` case-insensitively. There is **no dedicated count-by-city repository method** — `OwnerRepository` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`) only exposes `findByLastName`, `findById`, `save`, `findAll`, `findAll(Pageable)`, and `delete`. No `countByCity` exists.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/CityAtCapacityException.java`**
```java
public class CityAtCapacityException extends Exception {
    public CityAtCapacityException(String city, int capacity) {
        super("City at capacity: " + city + " already has " + capacity + " owners");
    }
}
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler.java`** — maps the exception to HTTP 409:
```java
public void handle(@Parameter CityAtCapacityException ex,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>> response) {
    ProblemDetail detail = ProblemDetails.build(ex, HttpStatus.CONFLICT, ex.getMessage());
    response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CONFLICT).body(detail));
}
```

Wired via **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.CityAtCapacityException.yml`**.

## 2. Owner creation/registration flow

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** defines the pipeline (authorize `OWNER_ADMIN`, all steps under `transaction` govern). Ordered chain:
`checkIdempotency → validateRegistrationDate → build → rejectDisposableEmail → validatePostcode → assignHousehold → ensureUniqueIdentity → assignCode → deduplicateCode → countNamesakes → capMembership → **ensureCityCapacity** → ensureDailyLimit → flagBulkSignup → flagPossibleDuplicate → save → recordIdempotency → audit → emitEvent → respond`

Note `ensureCityCapacity` runs **before** `save` (comment in the class: "a full city is a 409, not a persisted overflow"). The corresponding function classes all live under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. The terminal `respond` step is `RespondWithOwnerCreated`.

Other owner endpoint YAMLs: `owners.GET.yml`, `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`, `.PUT.yml`, `.DELETE.yml`, and `v2/owners.GET.yml`, all under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/`.

## 3. Response DTO(s) for owners

There is **no hand-written `OwnerResponse` class**. The response type is `OwnerDto`, **generated from the OpenAPI spec** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (schema `Owner`, which is `OwnerFields` + read-only derived fields). The create step builds it via MapStruct:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`**
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
    OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
}
```

`RespondWithOwner.java` (used by GET) does the same, returning `ObjectResponse<OwnerDto>`.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — the MapStruct interface that constructs `OwnerDto`. Every derived read-only field is an `@Mapping(... expression=...)` calling a helper in the `function.owner` package (e.g. `selfLink`, `displayName`, `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, `checkDigit`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`). It also defines `toOwner`, `toOwnerDtoCollection`, and a `toOwnerPageDto` default method.

The `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (lines ~2090-2257) defines all response fields: `id`, `selfLink`, `displayName`, `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `initials`, `salutation`, `locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`, `deleted`, `pets` (required). 

**Important gap:** there is **no `capacityWarning` field** in `openapi.yml`, in `OwnerMapper`, or anywhere in `src/main`.

## 4. Tests related to capacity / owner city counts

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — a single test that expects a **not-yet-implemented** `capacityWarning` field:
```java
/** capacity-warning: 'capacityWarning' is true when the owner's city already holds 40-49
 * owners (approaching the 50 hard limit). Fill a fresh city to 40, then the next owner in it warns. */
@Test
void coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity() throws Exception {
    String city = "Warn" + seq();
    fillCity(city, 40);
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("city", city);
    int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.capacityWarning").value(true));
}
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — the base harness. Relevant helpers: `fillCity(String city, int n)` (creates `n` unique owners all in the same city to drive per-city rules), `createOwnerOk`, `getOwner`, `ownerNode()`, `seq()`. Class is `@Transactional` so each test rolls back and only sees seed data plus what it creates. The class comment explicitly mentions the "per-city cap".

### Summary of the state of play
- The hard cap (50, 409 via `CityAtCapacityException`) is implemented in `EnsureCityCapacity`, counting by iterating `findAll()`.
- The **soft `capacityWarning` (40-49) is specified only by a failing/pending test** — it is not present in `openapi.yml`, `OwnerMapper`, the `Owner` model, or any function class. There is no field to populate it and no helper computing the 40-49 band.

